 "markdown": "## Summary\nI will add a \"Home\" button to the page header (before Next) by giving the overview-page template a `secondary-actions` entry and wiring its `on-sp-secondary-action` to a listener that runs the already-existing `GoHomeChain`.\n\n## How it works today\nThe page is drawn by `oj-sp-general-overview-page`, which shows only its own header plus whatever sits in its slots. The header currently has one button, the **Next** primary action (`primary-action='[[ {\"label\": \"Next\", \"display\": \"on\"} ]]'`, handled by `$listeners.nextToCatalog` → `NavigateToCatalogChain`). A `GoHomeChain.js` already exists (it navigates to the `home` page), left over from a previous change, but nothing on the page invokes it — there is no secondary action and no listener for it.\n\n## What changes\nA header **Home** button is shown before **Next**. Secondary actions render before the primary one on these templates, so declaring Home as a secondary action places it to the left of Next. It dispatches to `GoHomeChain` through a new `goHome` event listener.\n\n## The change\n- `project-create-request-page.json` — add a `goHome` event listener that calls `GoHomeChain`.\n- `project-create-request-page.html` — add `secondary-actions` and `on-sp-secondary-action` to the `oj-sp-general-overview-page`, dispatching the `home` action to `$listeners.goHome`.\n\n## After the change\n1. Open **Create Equipment Request**.\n2. In the page header you now see two buttons: **Home** (left) and **Next** (right).\n3. Click **Home** → `GoHomeChain` runs and navigates to the application home page.\n4. Click **Next** → behaves exactly as before (`NavigateToCatalogChain`).\n\n## Risks\n`GoHomeChain` navigates to a page named `home` within this flow context; if `home` is not reachable from here the navigation would fail. The chain already exists and is unchanged, so no other page is affected. None otherwise known.\n\n## How to test\n1. Go to `/vp/shell/customer-portal/project-create-request`.\n2. Confirm the header shows **Home** then **Next**.\n3. Click **Home**; confirm you land on the home page.\n4. Return to the page, fill required fields, click **Next**; confirm you reach Request Catalog as before.\n\n## Questions\nNone.",
